"""turboctl: tame Intel Turbo Boost and AMD Precision Boost instead of disabling them.

Usage:
  turboctl status                 show the CPU and the limits in place
  turboctl monitor                temperature, power, ratio and active limit, once a second
  turboctl apply [PROFILE]        apply PROFILE, or the saved profile
  turboctl set PROFILE            apply and save PROFILE (off, cool, stock or custom)
  turboctl undervolt MV           core and cache voltage offset, 0 to -100 mV (Intel)
  turboctl uvtest [FROM [TO]]     undervolt stability test, default -20 to -100 mV (Intel)
  turboctl serve                  JSON backend used by turboctl-gui
  turboctl watch                  keep the AMD power limits when the firmware raises them (service)
  turboctl update                 install the latest signed release, if newer (install.sh installs)
  turboctl update-interval [WHEN] check at boot and every 12h, daily, weekly, monthly, or never (default: as saved)
  turboctl clean-shutdown         run at shutdown by turboctl-shutdown.service
  turboctl --version

Supported: Intel Core 4th to 10th generation (Haswell to Comet Lake), up to 8 cores;
AMD Ryzen with the amd-pstate or acpi-cpufreq driver, plus power and temperature
limits on Ryzen 6000/7035 (Rembrandt), 7040/8040 (Phoenix, Hawk Point) and 200 series.
"""
